# Document titles

The document title, `og:title`, and `twitter:title` are `{title} – Blnk Docs` in sentence case. `title` is the page H1. The dash is an en dash.

Sentence case capitalizes the first word and lowercases the rest. Product names and acronyms stay capitalized: Blnk, Core, Cloud, Watch, Typesense, Go, Java, Python, TypeScript, Git, OAuth, API, SDK, CLI.

A page titled `Search` is `Search – Blnk Docs`. A page titled `Audit Logs` is `Audit logs – Blnk Docs`.

A title has to say what the page is. A changelog names the product and the changelog: `Go SDK changelog`. An overview names the subject: `Balances overview`. A quick start or error page names the language: `TypeScript quick start`, `Go error handling`. Leave `SDK` out of those titles.

Do not set `seoTitle`. Do not use `•`, `|`, `Blnk Developer Documentation`, `Blnk API Reference`, `Blnk Cloud Guide`, or another site name.
